      "writtenOn": "2022-06-02T13:45:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry to drag this review out, but after looking at this CL again, I figured out what\u0027s bothering me. This API:\n\n1) Requires users to know which variant of addOption/addChildOption to call, based on which *value* of SkShaderType they\u0027re using. That\u0027s not the end of the world by itself, except...\n2) It also encodes our internal decisions about which properties of each shader are important into the various signatures.\n\nWhat happens if we decide that having gradients use different shaders for different tile modes is worth it? Or when we have another shader type that happens to have two integers as the relevant payload? (eg: Perlin noise + min/max octaves?).\n\nI know we don\u0027t have a concrete SkShader instance we can pull from at this point (and I agree with that), but can we require that clients provide a superset of the information we need (at least the information that\u0027s common to all shader types), in all cases? That lets us adjust those decisions internally without changing the API every time. It also allows us to make some of those decisions configurable by the client (without changing the signature of these functions).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 135,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 137,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "d12e85c2f6992654f05bd6ed51bab0823d9fe40a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1643d3f_7e23ec4f",
        "filename": "src/core/SkCombinationBuilder.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 56
      },
      "lineNbr": 182,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-02T13:27:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d really suggest removing the memoization of these values, and just compute them every time they\u0027re requested:\n\n1) They\u0027re currently only used for debug (dump) code, and testing. I suspect that long-term, that\u0027s going to still be true? Clients may want to query once to check how they\u0027re doing, but unless we expect these to be requested many times, the memoization isn\u0027t saving us anything.\n\n2) As it stands now, if you add some options, then ask how many combinations there are, and then add more options... you get incorrect cached results from the builder. Eliminating the cache fixes that, too.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 181,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 182,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "d12e85c2f6992654f05bd6ed51bab0823d9fe40a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
